# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go build output
#
# Windows extensions matter here: `go build` in the repo root drops
# fact-extractor.exe beside main.go, outside dist/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binaries from `go test -c`, and the profiling/coverage files that
# `go test -coverprofile` and pprof leave behind.
*.test
*.test.exe
*.out
*.prof
*.pprof
coverage.*

# Go workspace files are a local development concern, never the project's.
go.work
go.work.sum

# stdlib only - if a vendor/ ever appears it is a mistake, not a commit.
vendor/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This project's own artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Downloaded release archives
.download/

# Build output and run artefacts
dist/
result.*
*.log

# Generated by build.ps1 into dist/, never committed. Modelfile* also covers
# Modelfile.gemma4, written for the --model alternate.
settings.json
Modelfile*

# The text being processed is the user's own
prompt.md

# Models are far too large for git
*.gguf
models/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows shell and editor debris
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
